WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.680
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and because I just
passed 250,000 subscribers I wanted to post

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.919
a nice shiny new Doctor Who video and say
thank you so much to all you guys. A lot of

00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:10.790
you guys have been asking for new Doctor Who
and the whole reason I started my channel

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:15.100
was to make a video for the Doctor Who Christmas
Special back in 2012. So why not make some

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.680
Doctor Who to celebrate.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.730
So this is going to be a Series 8 video with
a breakdown of all the new things happening

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.789
behind the scenes and what kind of Doctor
Who videos I'm going to be doing this summer.

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:27.930
But I wanted to start by asking a really important
question.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:31.060
How would you feel if Steven Moffat and the
Doctor Who team completely changed all the

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:36.129
rules. I'm talking about everything from the
way it looks to the original rules from Classic

00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:37.089
Who that form the Canon? Everything.

00:00:37.089 --> 00:00:41.569
Based on the comments I've seen most of you
guys are a little worried or just outright

00:00:41.569 --> 00:00:42.699
hate the idea.

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:46.489
The reason I ask is because Steven Moffat
has said that they're making the biggest changes

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:51.769
to the series since it came back in 2005.
Since he tends to exaggerate a little here's

00:00:51.769 --> 00:00:54.129
the top 5 five things I think that means

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:58.870
Number 5 - They're Going to Change The Number
Of Companions The Doctor Has At Any One Time

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:04.470
We know Clara is still a core companion, but
Danny Pink is going to be on board the TARDIS

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.990
for a large part of the season. Supposedly
starting after the first couple of episodes.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:13.990
And there's a rumor that Ellis George is playing
his sister and will also become a new companion.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.859
Her character's name is supposed to be Courtney.

00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:22.369
There were pictures from the set that show
her wearing the same space suit from that

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:24.060
outdoor scene on the beach.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.899
Since 2005 the Doctor has typically only had
one or two real companions at any one time.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:33.450
But the current record holder for total number
of companions is stil David Tennant with 11.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.049
But he would only travel with one or two of
them at any one time.

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:41.399
The Eighth Doctor also had a brother sister
Companion team named Gemma and Samson Griffin.

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:45.340
Who he met in a library during the Terra Firma
Audio Drama.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:49.640
Before the 50th Anniversary all of the non-tv
stuff wasn't really considered canon. I know

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.420
a lot of you guys were really happy when Steven
Moffat changed that.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.740
Number 4 - They're Going To Change How Previous
Doctor's Come Back

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.950
Old Doctor's coming back during a new Doctor's
run is something they've done in the Specials.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:04.249
But because of what happened in the 50th Anniversary
it seems like it's okay now for the Doctor

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:09.200
to interact with previous versions of himself
without the universe collapsing on itself.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:16.200
Matt Smith is supposedly going to be interacting
with Peter Capaldi 
in the first episode, via the whole Handles

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:28.170
phone call business from the Christmas Special.
Before this, during regular episodes whenever

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:32.400
previous Doctor's were featured it was either
with stock footage or other actors like in

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.780
the Series 7 finale.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:40.680
So now The Doctor will be able to speak to
other versions of himself. This time it's

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.290
really just a phone message, not a conversation.
But this is another new way to feature previous

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:50.150
Doctors. So everyone really wanting Classic
Doctor's to come back. This is a new backdoor.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:53.470
I know when you say come back though, what
you really mean is to come back on screen.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.430
But that's what Anniversary Specials are for.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:58.750
Matt Smith even said right after he wrapped
his last day he was bugging Steven Moffat

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:03.710
about how soon they could do another Anniversary
Special. Personally I think it will be five

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:06.240
years. But they could choose to celebrate
a different type of anniversary to get one

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.920
out sooner.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.000
Number 3 - They're going to change the Rules
The Doctor created for himself (the actual

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:12.150
rules)

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:15.120
When I say change the rules I'm talking about
the Doctor's own rules that he quotes. The

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.570
official rules have changed a few times but
with Capaldi it sounds like they're be changing

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.440
them in a really big way.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:27.370
Here's an example of some of the previous
changes to the first rule: I think the first

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:32.340
time we heard it was during the Fourth Doctor's
Run and his was "Do Exactly as I Say" that

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.570
was during the Ribos Operation in Season 16

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:39.930
Then the Seventh Doctor's first rule was "I'm
in Charge" which he said during Dragonfire

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.790
in season 24.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:46.260
The Ninth Doctor's Fist rule was "Don't Wander
Off" which he said in Empty Child in series

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:46.620
1

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.280
Then they didn't change that, David Tennant
and Matt Smith both used that as their first

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:56.610
rule too. Technically Matt Smith's Alternate
First Rule was "The Doctor Lies".

00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:00.350
So don't be surprised if Peter Capaldi changes
the First Rule again.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:04.470
Number 2 - They're going to radically alter
The Doctor's relationship with his companion

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.550
or companions

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:10.360
Each new Doctor changes the whole tone of
the show and the most visible way we see that

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:15.040
is in his relationship with his companion
or companions. Matt Smith's run was like a

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:20.850
Relationship comedy with universe ending consequences
like the big bang at the end of series 5.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:24.680
It was Amy, Rory and River stuck in an awkward
love triangle.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:30.150
Based on what we've seen from the set Clara
and Capaldi's Doctor are starting off on a

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:35.070
good foot. But steven moffat has said some
things that make me think they won't be best

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:39.800
buds by the end of the series like Donna Noble
and the Tenth Doctor were super buddies. I

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.790
guess you could say the Doctor has been good
friends with all his companions regardless

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:50.440
of romantic stuff going on. So giving Capaldi
and Clara are more tense dynamic would be

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:57.370
a big departure. That doesn't mean he's going
to be a straight up mean doctor though.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:02.320
But it's pretty clear they're subtracting
the romance. Not completely, but at least

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.740
the romance between Doctor and Companion.
.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:12.840
Number 1 - The Doctor will not be the dependable
hero we've known him and he will be way less

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.560
funny on purpose

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.160
I feel like this is the biggest change just
because the Doctor has always been a caregiver,

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:23.290
as the name implies. A doctor is a healer.
The War Doctor even said, "Physician, heal

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:26.520
thyself" when he regenerated at the end of
the 50th Anniversary episode.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:30.780
So what does it mean when the doctor isn't
dependable or as dependable as he's been in

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:36.620
the past? When Moffat suggested this I thought
of Matt Smith in Good Man Goes to War when

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:37.380
he saved Amy.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:41.830
They had that whole montage with Rory and
the twelfth Cyber Legion and there was no

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.710
doubt in your mind the Doctor would save her.
It's almost like he can't fail, like he's

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:49.160
so invincible that he unfurls the headless
monk robe and just declares Amy needs to grab

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.800
her coat so they can leave.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:56.450
Making the Doctor less dependable means Clara
and any other companions that join up are

00:05:56.450 --> 00:06:00.760
going to have to become a lot more independent.
This could mean them flying the TARDIS more

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:04.669
often or bailing The Doctor out of situations
rather than the reverse.

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:08.770
The Christmas Special did end with The Doctor
forgetting how to fly the TARDIS. I don't

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:13.750
think that was permanent, but I do think it
means he's going to be getting a lot of help

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.270
from Clara remembering things.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.610
But now it's your turn, let me know what you
think the biggest change in Series 8 is going

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:19.030
to be.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:25.450
Here's a quick update from the set. Clara
was just seen wielding Matt Smith's sonic,

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.660
they've completed filming a good portion of
the episodes so I'd say this is from one of

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:34.470
the later stories this series. The only other
companion I can remember who's used a sonic

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:35.960
was River Song.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:39.870
They also just announced Rachel Talalay will
direct the finale two episodes before the

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:45.780
christmas special. The finale is going to
be a two parter. We don't have any info on

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:46.940
the christmas special yet.

